Chapter: EffectLaunderPartial
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (effect rows stage 0). Partial application:
 the effect row lives on the LAST arrow of a curried chain, so a
 partially applied effectful function has the same effectful shape
 as a plain one. The CL 6494 concrete-parameter check should
 already reject passing it where a pure function is required
 (CDX2031); this probe pins that the partial-application path does
 not slip past it.

Section: Definitions

  log-add : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  log-add (a) (b) = act
    print-line-uni "adding"
    a + b
  end

  apply-pure : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  apply-pure (f) (x) = f x

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (apply-pure (log-add 1) 2))
  end
